Now we need to establish clearance nominial: establish_clearance_nominal SCB CC_A LB TL (requires candidate_loading_verified SCB, candidate_compliance_certificate_linked SCB CC_A, candidate_loading_container_linked SCB LB, loading_container_leg_linked LB TL, not origin_leg_loaded TL, not destination_leg_loaded TL, not candidate_clearance_established SCB). We have all: loading_verified true, compliance linked true (we assigned), loading container linked true, loading container leg linked true, origin_leg_loaded false, destination_leg_loaded false, candidate_clearance_established false. So we can establish clearance.

After that, candidate_clearance_established SCB true.

Now we need to set dispatch allocated for OA, DA, SCB, and dispatch ready, and dispatched.

We already have dispatch_allocated SCA true, dispatch_ready SCA true, dispatched SCA true from init. But we need dispatch_allocated for OA, DA, SCB.

We also need dispatch_ready for OA, DA, SCB, and dispatched for those.

We have dispatch_slot_alpha available initially. We need to link dispatch slot to each candidate (OA, DA, SCB) and allocate dispatch slot for each. However note that dispatch_slot is a resource; we can only allocate it to one candidate at a time because allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate consumes dispatch_slot_available (sets not dispatch_slot_available). After allocating to one candidate, dispatch_slot becomes unavailable. We need to allocate to three candidates (OA, DA, SCB). But we have only one dispatch slot? Actually we have only dispatch_slot_alpha object. The goal requires candidate_dispatch_slot_linked for OA, DA, SCB all to dispatch_slot_alpha. That would mean the same dispatch slot linked to three candidates simultaneously. However the allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate action sets candidate_dispatch_slot_linked and consumes dispatch_slot_available (makes it unavailable). It does not prevent linking same slot to multiple candidates? The effect includes candidate_dispatch_slot_linked ?candidate ?dispatch_slot and not dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot. If we allocate to second candidate, the precondition requires dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot, which would be false after first allocation. So we cannot allocate the same slot to multiple candidates. However goal requires all three linked to same slot. This seems contradictory unless the domain allows multiple candidates to share a dispatch slot (maybe dispatch_slot is not a resource that gets consumed? But the action removes availability. Could there be multiple dispatch slots? Only one defined. Perhaps we misinterpret: The goal may require each candidate to have a dispatch slot linked, but they could be different slots? However they all specify dispatch_slot_alpha. Could be a mistake but we must satisfy goal as given.

